# The repo's canonical text form is LF, enforced at checkout too: no smudge
# boundary between working tree and repo, so byte-level gates (git diff
# --cached --check in the pre-commit whitespace job, verify-* comparisons,
# translation-pairing hashes) see one form on every host.
# If a file class ever genuinely needs CRLF in the working tree (.bat/.cmd
# for cmd.exe), add a `*.bat text eol=crlf` override AFTER this line — the
# in-repo form stays LF; CRLF becomes checkout-time presentation only.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts: CRLF in the working tree for cmd.exe / pwsh, the
# in-repo form stays LF so the byte-level gates above see one form.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary fixtures: kept byte-for-byte, never renormalized.
*.3mf binary
*.pdf binary
# STEP files are generated by CAD kernels (OCCT/CadQuery) with kernel-native
# line endings and insignificant trailing whitespace; they are semantic
# fixtures (compared via compareStepFiles, never byte-diffed), so treat them
# as byte-for-byte data like the other binary fixtures.
*.step binary